{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558787-v5-and-w5-hard-to-kill-aspect","id":1558787,"title":"V5 and W5 hard to kill aspect","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-03-11T03:11:59-07:00","id":1558787,"title":"V5 and W5 hard to kill aspect","content":"I've never played V5 or W5 (yet), but i have both books and the survivability of Vampires and Werewolves seems a bit extreme, no?<br /> According to W5 the only way to definitly kill a werewolf is fire, silver or complete destruction of his body (cutting his head off seems pretty definitive too)<br /> V5 say that the only way to kill a vampire is fire, daylight, decapitaton and body destruction (using acid as an exemple in the book)<br /> <br /> Aside from those any other aggr damage, upgraded from bashing or directly inflicted, can be healed over time. Of course the system is different than V20 edition, keeping only 2 types of damage but the general health idea is still the same, some wound are worst than others and need more time to heal.<br /> <br /> On one hand it make these creature scarier and more myth accurate, on the other hand it means that in game using fire and their specific weakness is the only way to kill them<br /> <br /> I'm just curious of how it is percieved in the community, do you think it's good/bad or just a specific mechanic that work because it is designed for V5 gaming rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T04:02:09-07:00","id":1558789,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's that much discussion about this specific aspect of things... or at least not in places I hang out (which means not places that are exclusively WoD5 focused).<br /> <br /> From back in the V5 playtest era, my impression was very much that there's a bit of a disconnect between the description and the rules. In the descriptions of how enduring they are, killing them seems hard. In the actual rules? Sure harder than squishy mortals, but not so hard.<br /> <br /> I think some of that came from the initial concept of tuning conflicts into 3-rounds of rolling. If two vampires are fighting to the final death, and after three rounds one is clearly outmatching their opponent, the idea is that you stop rolling and then move on to narrating the execution. So &quot;doing massive damage&quot; doesn't really need a lot of mechanical rigor to it, it's just meant to guide what describing that looks like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T04:03:11-07:00","id":1558790,"title":"","content":"In W5, I would argue, one of the issues is that the situation is the complete opposite of &quot;hard to kill&quot;. Especially in the beginning when players aren't familiar with all the systems. Some of the punishing mechanics can sneak up on you and disrupt things. For example, you gotta be careful in managing your character's Willpower and Rage. For example, using Gifts and Rites requires either Rage checks (you roll a die, 6 or better nothing happens, 5 or lower you use a dot of Rage) or spending Willpower. But if that lands you at Rage 0, you enter a state called &quot;losing the wolf&quot;. In that state, you can't shapeshift into anything other than Homid or Lupus and you can't use Gifts and Rites. And the only way to get out of that is to howl at the moon at night. Unless you have a specific Rite... but of course you can't use the Rite when the PC with the Rite has &quot;lost the wolf&quot; themselves, for example. Also, it means that landing at Rage 0 during combat is really bad. The Willpower-cost is another tricky thing because once you enter the Umbra, you have to spend a point of Willpower at the start of every scene or you will take a point of Aggravated Damage. And the Umbra Agg-Damage is another thing that will kill Garou (well, it turns your character into a bad Spirit but technically you lose your character is what that means). This then is also compounded by Willpower being very important for when Frenzy occurs (if you fail two Willpower tests, your character is supposed to fight everything in sight until the Frenzied character is the only thing left standing). <br /> <br /> My experience as ST with W5 is that it's a tough balancing act. On one hand, in the few turns where a PC might use their Crinos Form they can dish out a lot of damage and if you have multiple PCs use their Crinos Form, it's tough to create a respectable foe. But on the other hand, if a player didn't manage their Rage right and ends up at Rage 0 during combat, then that character immediately becomes pretty useless and then any enemy that was created with the Crinos Form in mind will easily kill that PC. And even with the Crinos Form... since Regeneration triggers Rage checks, that is yet another way a character might end up at Rage 0 during combat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T06:26:11-07:00","id":1558791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558787-v5-and-w5-hard-to-kill-aspect#post1558787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've never played V5 or W5 (yet), but i have both books and the survivability of Vampires and Werewolves seems a bit extreme, no?<br /> According to W5 the only way to definitly kill a werewolf is fire, silver or complete destruction of his body (cutting his head off seems pretty definitive too)<br /> V5 say that the only way to kill a vampire is fire, daylight, decapitaton and body destruction (using acid as an exemple in the book)<br /> <br /> Aside from those any other aggr damage, upgraded from bashing or directly inflicted, can be healed over time. Of course the system is different than V20 edition, keeping only 2 types of damage but the general health idea is still the same, some wound are worst than others and need more time to heal.<br /> <br /> On one hand it make these creature scarier and more myth accurate, on the other hand it means that in game using fire and their specific weakness is the only way to kill them<br /> <br /> I'm just curious of how it is percieved in the community, do you think it's good/bad or just a specific mechanic that work because it is designed for V5 gaming rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>If they were myth accurate, you'd need a whole damn ritual to kill a vampire.<br /> <br /> Stake the heart.<br /> <br /> Cut off the head.<br /> <br /> Stuff the body with garlic.<br /> <br /> Bless it with holy water.<br /> <br /> Nail them face down in their coffin, so the next time they try to escape, they descend to Hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T09:32:14-07:00","id":1558794,"title":"","content":"My concern is mainly that the RAW say that werewolves and vampire loosing their last health box as aggr fall unconscious/torpor, and begin healing. They die only if you use fire, decapitation, complete body destruction, daylight for one and silver for the other.<br /> <br /> In 20th edition a werewolf slashing and biting a vampire is a direct kill, in W5 werewolves bite can be healed if the vampire is left on the ground (very unlikely i know but still) without being burned, decapitated or reduced to a pile of bloody flesh","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T10:13:45-07:00","id":1558795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558787-v5-and-w5-hard-to-kill-aspect?p=1558794#post1558794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My concern is mainly that the RAW say that werewolves and vampire loosing their last health box as aggr fall unconscious/torpor, and begin healing. They die only if you use fire, decapitation, complete body destruction, daylight for one and silver for the other.<br /> <br /> In 20th edition a werewolf slashing and biting a vampire is a direct kill, in W5 werewolves bite can be healed if the vampire is left on the ground (very unlikely i know but still) without being burned, decapitated or reduced to a pile of bloody flesh</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm gonna focus on the W5-side of things here... In W5 the &quot;losing the wolf&quot;-status matters a lot. I had that happen in the oneshot I was running. Because W5 has so many punitive mechanics, things just pile up.<br /> <br /> As it's described on pg. 134, you get this:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Garou who has been incapacitated by Aggravated damage is taken out of action and falls unconscious, unless they\u2019re able to regenerate at least one point of Aggravated damage. (This can be done even if unconscious, <b>providing they have enough Rage</b>.) If allowed to rest for a night they also regenerate one Aggravated health level automatically, as normal, but if they Sustain aggravated damage from fire or silver before resting, they die. </div> </div> </div>I highlighted the important bit here. Because here's the issue with W5. Yes, technically only silver, complete bodily destruction/decapitation, fire and being in the Umbra too long will kill a Garou. But here's what's going to happen if you get to this point with no Rage. Your tracker is filled up with Agg-Damage, the character falls unconscious, for whatever reason the enemy is prevented from giving the character the true death-blow, they're allowed to rest for the night and regenerate one health-level. BUT... since they have no Rage, they've &quot;lost the wolf&quot; which means until the next night when they can howl at the moon, the character can't use Regeneration, can't shift into the &quot;supernatural Forms&quot; and can't use Gifts or Rites. The character is just a normal human or normal wolf until that time. So, a character might not die but it will take quite a while before the character is back to being a functional Garou. <br /> <br /> And with any WtA-game, getting into combat is far more common than with a VtM-game, I would say. <br /> <br /> Overall, both a vampire in Torpor and a Garou who has &quot;lost the wolf&quot; are pretty easy targets unless there are others around who protect them in that weakened state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T13:05:24-07:00","id":1558801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558787-v5-and-w5-hard-to-kill-aspect?p=1558791#post1558791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If they were myth accurate, you'd need a whole damn ritual to kill a vampire.<br /> <br /> Stake the heart.<br /> <br /> Cut off the head.<br /> <br /> Stuff the body with garlic.<br /> <br /> Bless it with holy water.<br /> <br /> Nail them face down in their coffin, so the next time they try to escape, they descend to Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which myth? V:tM does lean heavily on Dracula, but it also has sunlight actually burn vampires instead of just de-power them down to mortal levels. In the novel, they flat out just stab him with knives when it's day out. The Count doesn't even get direct kill in; Quincy dies fighting his minority henchmen and not him.<br /> <br /> And with werewolves, mind, the &quot;Which myth?&quot; question intensifies, because the Garou are both something far flung in inspiration and synthesized for the needs of their own setting. That's not even really remarkable as far as werewolves go, either; it seems that the people of old were like we are with Lunar Exalted in the modern times, and few people could ever agree on what a werewolf &quot;should&quot; be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T14:09:11-07:00","id":1558804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558787-v5-and-w5-hard-to-kill-aspect?p=1558801#post1558801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which myth? V:tM does lean heavily on Dracula, but it also has sunlight actually burn vampires instead of just de-power them down to mortal levels. In the novel, they flat out just stab him with knives when it's day out. The Count doesn't even get direct kill in; Quincy dies fighting his minority henchmen and not him.<br /> <br /> And with werewolves, mind, the &quot;Which myth?&quot; question intensifies, because the Garou are both something far flung in inspiration and synthesized for the needs of their own setting. That's not even really remarkable as far as werewolves go, either; it seems that the people of old were like we are with Lunar Exalted in the modern times, and few people could ever agree on what a werewolf &quot;should&quot; be.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the whole basis for why there are different clans / tribes in the first place. Each one representing different aspects of the mythos.<br /> <br /> Or, at least, that was the case in the Chronicles setting. Kind of got a bit ridiculous in World of Darkness, when they were trying to turn practically anything into its own vampire bloodline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T14:20:54-07:00","id":1558805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558787-v5-and-w5-hard-to-kill-aspect?p=1558795#post1558795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The character is just a normal human or normal wolf until that time. So, a character might not die but it will take quite a while before the character is back to being a functional Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolves don't die but stay out of action for a long period, pretty much like vampire's torpor if i get it right, leaving them vulnerable to killing blow for a long time. It's the part &quot;If allowed to rest for a night they also regenerate one Aggravated health level automatically, as normal&quot; that is confusing (unless i missed a line somewhere), it suggest that werewolves heal 1 aggr damage per day without rage check, but according to you it does not apply if they lose the wolf?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-11T14:46:05-07:00","id":1558807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558787-v5-and-w5-hard-to-kill-aspect?p=1558794#post1558794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 20th edition a werewolf slashing and biting a vampire is a direct kill, in W5 werewolves bite can be healed if the vampire is left on the ground (very unlikely i know but still) without being burned, decapitated or reduced to a pile of bloody flesh</div> </div> </div> </div>This feels like a bit of an overstatement.<br /> <br /> A W20 is by no means guaranteed a fatal blow on a vampire just because they have easy access to agg in their best combat forms. In 20th, characters don't die unless they take more damage beyond what it takes to fill them to Incapacitated. If a vampire takes too much damage, they fall into torpor and can heal unless someone makes sure to finish them off. The descriptions of what it takes to do so haven't really changed either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-12T03:05:36-07:00","id":1558816,"title":"","content":"Just checked and you're right, in v20 the final death occur if the vampire suffer aggr while incapacitated. Yet it does not specify those aggr must be fire or sunray to effectively destroy it, unlike w5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-12T10:22:07-07:00","id":1558823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558787-v5-and-w5-hard-to-kill-aspect?p=1558804#post1558804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's kind of the whole basis for why there are different clans / tribes in the first place. Each one representing different aspects of the mythos.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires in V:tM never evade the &quot;immolated at dawn&quot; part of their mythos. There are certain bits that they can't avoid and which are still held in common.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, that was never the intention behind the tribes. Development in W5 seemed to have pitched a fit about it and why it wasn't more like Vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or, at least, that was the case in the Chronicles setting. Kind of got a bit ridiculous in World of Darkness, when they were trying to turn practically anything into its own vampire bloodline. </div> </div> </div>The V:tM method of deciding splats really showing its shortcomings there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-12T10:44:22-07:00","id":1558826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558787-v5-and-w5-hard-to-kill-aspect?p=1558816#post1558816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just checked and you're right, in v20 the final death occur if the vampire suffer aggr while incapacitated. Yet it does not specify those aggr must be fire or sunray to effectively destroy it, unlike w5.</div> </div> </div> </div>As I understand it, 5th edition has done away with Bashing / Lethal damage and now just has Superficial and Aggravated.<br /> <br /> Which means that most of the damage a vampire is likely to receive will be Superficial, which they can very easily repair themselves from.<br /> <br /> Without fire, sunlight, or supernatural enhancements, you need to royally fuck them up before the damage converts to Aggravated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-12T11:13:29-07:00","id":1558827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558787-v5-and-w5-hard-to-kill-aspect?p=1558816#post1558816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just checked and you're right, in v20 the final death occur if the vampire suffer aggr while incapacitated. Yet it does not specify those aggr must be fire or sunray to effectively destroy it, unlike w5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but WoD5's reduction to two damage types is kinda the thing here more than not.<br /> <br /> To the point from V20: &quot;An incapacitated or torpid vampire may also be sent to Final Death through massive amounts of bashing or lethal trauma (decapitated, trapped under a 10-ton rock, fed into a wood chipper, caught at ground zero of an explosion, crushed by deep-sea pressure, etc.). Typically, this damage must be enough to destroy or dismember the corpse beyond repair.&quot;<br /> <br /> In 20th, it's presumed that the damage is enough to meet the bar V5 sets by virtue of dealing the damage having to be described that way. So the idea of things beyond fire and sunlight are present in both sets of rules. The rules aren't 100% the same, but I they're not that different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-13T18:25:25-07:00","id":1558846,"title":"","content":"In short, this part doesn't really have any more impact in V5 than it did in V20, it's just worded differently but with similar result.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-14T22:21:49-07:00","id":1558863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cain Loup-Noir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558787-v5-and-w5-hard-to-kill-aspect?p=1558846#post1558846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In short, this part doesn't really have any more impact in V5 than it did in V20, it's just worded differently but with similar result.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in V20, it was really, really difficult to kill a vampire through Bashing damage. You only had to spend a single blood point to heal 2 points of Bashing.<br /> <br /> To kill a vampire through it, you'd need to fill all their health boxes with Bashing, before it started to inflict Lethal damage. Then you had to fill it all up with Lethal before it would upgrade to Aggravated.<br /> <br /> So, yeah, if you planned to kill a vampire by beating it to death with a baseball bat, you'd probably be exhausted by the time it finally died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-17T11:18:18-07:00","id":1558912,"title":"","content":"&quot;Good - I like my playthings EXTRA DURABLE.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T20:10:12-07:00","id":1558928,"title":"","content":"Oh the hours......days.......weeks......months of &quot;fun' debate there was on what exactly constitutes total bodily destruction........<br /> <br /> The consensus was RAW W5 Garou can't be killed by drowning, decapitation, starvation, sub zero temperatures, being drawn and quartered, flayed, thirst, removal of all internal organs, being half-fed into a wood chipper ( being wholly fed was a subject of great debate) etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-18T21:01:12-07:00","id":1558929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558787-v5-and-w5-hard-to-kill-aspect?p=1558928#post1558928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">being half-fed into a wood chipper ( being wholly fed was a subject of great debate) etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's to debate? Feeding somebody's entire body through a wood chipper would effectively juice them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-03-21T18:37:19-07:00","id":1558965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1558787-v5-and-w5-hard-to-kill-aspect?p=1558928#post1558928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The consensus was RAW W5 Garou can't be killed by drowning, decapitation, starvation, sub zero temperatures, being drawn and quartered, flayed, thirst, removal of all internal organs, being half-fed into a wood chipper ( being wholly fed was a subject of great debate) etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>While in V20 a garou incapacitated by lethal damage die if he suffer any more damage and his only chance or survive if incapacitated by aggr is a Rage roll. That's why W5 seems to make them extremely hard to kill","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26839-cain-loup-noir","name":"Cain Loup-Noir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26839_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"390"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-17T18:42:03-07:00","id":1561863,"title":"","content":"I actually think they're not durable enough for my tastes, yet.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing: the character is incapacitated, and will remain so for the foreseeable future. If you're there to kill them and you know what they are... That's it, isn't?<br /> <br /> None of the methods is particularly hard against an unmoving body. You know what you're doing, how to do it, and want to do it. You do it.<br /> <br /> Which situations would really, in practice, save their sorry ass?<br /> 1. Rescue,<br /> 2. Mercy,<br /> 3. The assailant is ignorant or it was an accident.<br /> <br /> Seriously, do you think those creatures should die easily in those situations? Or taking them out of combat for a considerable amount of time is enough?<br /> <br /> Myself, I think the later. And I would go for the whole ritual, I don't like any main splat having an easier time at bypassing each other's immortality, no kill without heavy commitment.<br /> <br /> And I'm not talking myths. In the folkloric sense there's no such a thing for vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}